<Base title="Research — AI × Garments" description="Research direction for responsible AI-assisted garment knowledge retrieval and pattern-making decision support."><section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">Research · AI × garments</p><h1>Preserving technical memory without <em>automating away judgment.</em></h1><p class="lead narrow">My long-term research theme is a garment knowledge assistant that helps teams retrieve relevant, validated historical learning while protecting confidential source material.</p></section><section class="research-map"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow light">Concept model</p><div class="map-row"><span>Comments</span><span>Images</span><span>Sample stage</span><span>Pattern action</span><span>Outcome</span></div><div class="map-core"><small>Structured, permission-aware knowledge layer</small><strong>Relevant precedent<br/>with evidence and confidence</strong></div><div class="map-row output"><span>Retrieve</span><span>Compare</span><span>Explain</span><span>Decide</span></div></div></section><section class="shell section-space"><SectionHead eyebrow="Research questions" title="The hard problems are technical and human."/><div class="capability-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Taxonomy</h3><p>How should knowledge be indexed across style, design, sample stage, issue, action and result?</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Evidence quality</h3><p>How can the system keep assignments, proposals, completed actions and validated outcomes distinct?</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Confidentiality</h3><p>How can useful relationships be preserved while employer and buyer sources remain restricted?</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Human judgment</h3><p>How should retrieved precedent support—not replace—the accountable technical professional?</p></article></div></section><section class="shell split section-space"><SectionHead eyebrow="Current status" title="A research concept, not a production product."/><div class="prose"><p>The taxonomy and evidence model are being developed through structured professional records. No claim is made that the system currently diagnoses fit, generates production-ready patterns or replaces a pattern maker.</p><p>The next meaningful milestones are a safe sample dataset, retrieval evaluation criteria, permission classes and a small prototype that always shows provenance and uncertainty.</p><a class="button" href="/projects/garment-knowledge-retrieval">Read the concept study →</a></div></section></Base>
